# Every change gets a review from a maintainer. AppHub is a credential-vending
# project heading for public release, so there is no path that merges without
# one.
#
# Ownership is a team, not a person: a review path through one individual is a
# bus factor of one, and a public repository should not advertise whose inbox to
# aim at.
#
# NOTE: CODEOWNERS binds only when the named team exists and has write access to
# this repository, and it is enforced only when branch protection requires
# code-owner review. The team has write access to the public repository; the
# private development repository sits in another organization, where it does
# not bind. Code-owner review is not required anywhere yet -- see
# docs/decisions/, "CI is a floor, not a gate, until branch protection is
# enabled".
*                       @conductorone/apphub-maintainers

# The gates themselves. A change that weakens CI, an import boundary, the
# disclosure rules, or the licence terms should be harder to land than a change
# those gates are protecting.
/.github/               @conductorone/apphub-maintainers
/.gitleaks.toml         @conductorone/apphub-maintainers
/Makefile               @conductorone/apphub-maintainers
/hack/                  @conductorone/apphub-maintainers
/internal/boundary/     @conductorone/apphub-maintainers
/internal/hermetic/     @conductorone/apphub-maintainers
/LICENSE                @conductorone/apphub-maintainers
/NOTICE                 @conductorone/apphub-maintainers
/SECURITY.md            @conductorone/apphub-maintainers
/docs/decisions/        @conductorone/apphub-maintainers
